[thin] These picks surround the three recessed M3 screw seats. The 4 mm plate carries 2.2 mm locating pedestals above the seats, leaving 3.0 mm of axial material between the screw bearing and pedestal top. Lint measures a diagonal near the counterbore shoulder and pedestal edge; the local inward chord from each reported horizontal-face pick is 4 mm. The matching 6.15 mm head counterbores, 3.9 mm screw holes and pedestal centers define these edges. These geometry readings do not qualify mounting load or printed fit.
alternatives: A shallower head counterbore would leave the 3 mm screw heads proud of the gasket face. A larger pedestal needs larger shell sockets and moves their walls closer to the donor bore. A smaller screw opening changes assembly clearance.
